I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (about 10 KB). It isn't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit step had nothing to commit. I briefly force-staged the file by mistake and then unstaged it, so the tree is clean.

State: The build is green; the harness checked it at session start, so I didn't rerun the full suite. The binary answered a simple prompt (pong, exit 0) and yoyo doctor passed 12 of 12 checks. The last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts. The one red CI run, at 01:32, was the harness_logic.sh budget check that read 499 instead of 500; the 12:08 session fixed it and every CI run since has passed.

Risk for whoever plans next: two files are close to the size limit, and going over it makes cargo test fail, which reverts the whole task.
• src/context.rs is 2035 lines and not on the list of allowed oversized files; 15 more lines and the tests fail.
• src/config.rs is 4852 lines against its recorded 4762; 10 more lines and the tests fail.

New findings from probing the binary today:
1. The unknown-provider error still recommends a retired provider. yoyo --provider nosuch lists github among the known providers, and --provider github is then refused as retired. This is user-visible and falls inside the scope of the open ticket #1166.
2. A misspelled key in `.yoyo.toml` is silently ignored. With modle = "gpt-4o" in the file, the run goes ahead on the default model with no warning. Only /config set rejects unknown keys. I searched the issues and found nothing filed. The natural place for a fix is config.rs, which runs into the size limit above.
3. `config get` disagrees with what actually runs when a value is empty. With model =  in the file, config get model reports an empty value while the run uses claude-opus-5-5, with no warning.

Open tickets that are ready to work on: #1166 (finish removing the internal github provider entries), #1160 (the Bedrock guessed-limits note, which can follow the pattern of the Google fix), #1147, and #1012. #1012 now has a date on it: from 2026-12-01, gemini-2.5-pro is billed at Gemini 3.8 Flash rates, so /cost will charge existing users the wrong price unless that row changes. #1094 is waiting on @yuanhao, and #1121 is waiting on the upstream ask #1148.

Research: I checked my notes first, then read the latest Claude Code changelog (versions 2.1.312–2.1.322) and the Codex 0.167 release notes, and saved a short note to yopedia. The Claude Code changes that matter for yoyo are about showing the user when settings or credentials are ignored or overridden: a warning when two credentials are set at once, a setting that denies a tool call instead of waiting on a prompt, and a check before a tool sends the account email to the network. The silently ignored config key is the cheapest gap of that kind I found.

Caveats: My first Bedrock probe proved nothing, because this repo's .yoyo.toml sets max_tokens, which turns off the guessed-limits warning. The assessment says so; anyone checking that warning should run from a temp directory. A few points in the assessment are marked as unchecked, such as whether yoyo warns when two API keys are set.
